
@0 = ~Kurosaï the Combiner~
@1 = ~Kurosaï~
@2 = ~Hello, dear customer. What can Kurosaï do for you today?~
@3 = ~That depends. What do you have to offer?~
@4 = ~Kurosaï offers nothing less than his skill and magic, inherited from the venerable master Ibunibï-Saï, which allow him to create powerful magical items from lesser ones.~
@5 = ~You mean you can combine several items to make a better one?~
@6 = ~Exactly. Kurosaï can take your +1 items and turn them into +2 items, or your +4 items and turn them into +5 items. It's up to you. You hand over the items, you pay, and Kurosaï gives you a better item. Simple.~
@7 = ~I see. What kinds of items can you improve?~
@8 = ~Kurosaï knows rituals for every kind of item, but he only works with enchantments. Three items for one with a higher enchantment: that is the formula. The price in gold is the square of the enchantment you want, multiplied by one thousand. You want a +3 bow? Then give Kurosaï three +2 bows and 9000 gold pieces.~
@9 = ~I understand. I'll come back when I need your services.~
@10 = ~Can you also improve special items?~
@11 = ~Yes. Kurosaï can also improve bracers of defense. Unfortunately, that is all. The venerable master Ibunibï-Saï knew other secrets, but Lady Death took him before he could teach them to Kurosaï. May he find bliss in the hot springs of the spirit realm.~
@12 = ~All right. I'll be back.~
@13 = ~Here is your new item. Thank you, dear customer.~
@14 = ~I don't need anything. Sorry to disturb you.~
@15 = ~Kurosaï! What are you doing here?~
@16 = ~Kurosaï has traveled far and will travel farther still. Trademeet was one stop; Saradush is another.~
@17 = ~Good to see you. I'll probably need your services again.~
@18 = ~Kurosaï also appears in Amkethran (cheat)~
@19 = ~You must install Kurosaï the Combiner before installing this component.~
@20 = ~Recipes cost less but require rare gems~
@21 = ~Kurosaï knows rituals for every kind of item, but he only works with enchantments. Three items for one with a higher enchantment: that is the formula. The price in gold is twice the enchantment you want, multiplied by one thousand, plus a rare gem. You want a +3 bow? Then give Kurosaï three +2 bows, a diamond, and 6000 gold pieces.~
@22 = ~An extra +1 item of each type in Shadows of Amn~
@23 = ~Kurosaï also appears at the Nashkel Carnival~
@24 = ~This mod requires BG2EE or EET.~
@25 = ~This component requires EET.~

